---
title: Create a shipment
description: Book a shipment, check it, and cancel it before pickup.
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

This guide is for the **shipper** role. The consoles call the Shipments API on the mock server; calls need an access token with `shipments:read` or `shipments:write`.

{% callout type="info" title="Reading is not calling" %}
Reviewers can read this page too, but their token has no Shipments permission, so every **Try** returns `403`. That's on purpose: see [Authentication](/docs/authentication).
{% /callout %}

## Book it

{% steps %}
{% step title="Quote the price" %}
Get a quote from the public [Rates API](/docs/rates) and keep its `id`.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Create the shipment" %}
Send the addresses, the parcels and the `quote_id`. Use a new `Idempotency-Key` per shipment, so a retried request can't book it twice.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Print the label" %}
Download it with `GET /shipments/{shipmentId}/label` as PDF, PNG or ZPL.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

{% api-operation spec="shipments" path="/shipments" method="post" /%}

## Check it

{% api-operation spec="shipments" path="/shipments/{shipmentId}" method="get" /%}

## Cancel it

Only before pickup; afterwards you get `409`.

{% api-operation spec="shipments" path="/shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel" method="post" /%}
